---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy notice | ${site.name}`}
  description="How this website and its owner handle your information."
>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="wrap privacy">
    <p class="privacy__draft-flag">
      Draft — this notice has not been finalised or reviewed. It describes the site as it currently
      works. Update it before taking on paid client work or collecting any personal data beyond a
      direct enquiry.
    </p>

    <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="privacy__updated">Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.</p>

    <h2>Who this covers</h2>
    <p>
      This notice covers this website, run by {site.founder} trading as {site.name} (a working name
      — see the footer for current contact details). Gurman has not yet registered as a sole trader;
      that is planned before any paid work begins.
    </p>

    <h2>This site itself</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts of any kind.
      It is a static set of pages: visiting it does not create an account, a session or a tracking
      profile. If analytics are added later, this notice will be updated first and a cookie or
      consent notice will be added if required.
    </p>

    <h2>If you get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      The "Get your free presence audit" links, and the pricing enquiry links, open your own email
      app (a <code>mailto:</code> link), your phone's dialler, or WhatsApp. Nothing you type is sent
      to or stored by this website — it goes directly from your device to Gurman's inbox, phone or
      WhatsApp, the same as it would if you'd looked up the details yourself. That message is then
      handled the same way as any other business enquiry: kept only as long as needed to answer you
      and, if you become a client, as part of the project record.
    </p>

    <h2>If you become a client</h2>
    <p>
      Any project involving an AI assistant, booking system or similar tool will have its own,
      specific explanation of what data is collected, which providers process it, and how long it is
      kept, agreed with you before launch. Health-related businesses (for example dental or
      physiotherapy clients) get extra care here, in line with the rules for special-category data.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what information is held about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or
      raise a concern, by contacting{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. If you're not satisfied
      with the response, you can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
    </p>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: var(--space-7);
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  .privacy__draft-flag {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .privacy__updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
